1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LeVang's Jun 28 1917
2 CONT
2 CONT ==DEATH OF A PIONEER LADY==
2 CONT Last Friday, at the Elstad church south of Lanesboro, took place the funeral of Mrs. Bertha Topness, one of Amherst township's oldest pioneer ladies. The remains had been brought back to the old home county from Wolford, N. D., wh
2 CONC ere she died on June 18th at the home of her son, S. S. Topness. She had been there only for a few short weeks, when she was taken suddenly ill with acute indigestion and died within a few hours. At the funeral the Revs. N. S. Mag
2 CONC elssen and John B. Rockne officiated, and there was a great gathering of friends and neighbors to show the deceased the last sad honors.
2 CONT
2 CONT The late Mrs. Topness was 85 years old on March 6th this year, having been born in Stavanger, Norway, in 1832. As a young girl she was married to the late Mr. Sylfest Topness, and they came to the United States a few years afterwa
2 CONC rds. After living on Jefferson Prairie, Wisconsin, for a short time the young couple came to Fillmore county and settled on a farm in Amherst township in the late fifties. The husband died eighteen years ago, and since then the wi
2 CONC dow has been making her home most of the time with a daughter, Mrs. Betsy Kolstad, at Highland. She was beloved, honored and respected by all who knew her, and she will be missed by many.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased is survived by the following children: Lars Topness and Mrs. Kolstad of Highland, Severin S. Topness, Mrs. Chas. Lawston, and Tollef S. Topness of Wolford, N. D., also by 21 grandchildren and 13 great grandchildren. All h
2 CONC er children and also one grandson, Selmer Topness of Wolford, were in attendance at the funeral.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha's parents were Lars Olsen and Britta Sjursdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT Elstad Lutheran Church burial records, p. 231 #14, Mrs. Bertha Topness 87 aar died 18 Juni 1917 buried 25 Juni 1917 at Elstad Hjemstavn: Elstad Note: Blotsygen fra ? Døde hos sin søn i Wolford N. D.
2 CONT
