1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Martin Johnson and my maternal great-grandma Cudelia Johnson were brother/sister. My great-grandma married Axel Melberg, and they lived in Norway, Iowa. I have great-grandpa Axel's chest that was the only thing that he brought wit
2 CONC h him from Norway country when he was about 22 yrs old (I'm looking at it now....love it!!). Axel and Cudelia "Delia" had 11 kids (2 died as babies). My grandpa Milo was the youngest. My mom, Lois was the oldest of Milo and Elizab
2 CONC eth's 3 children. As for the picture of Martin, it was from a genealogy book that my 2nd cousin's wife put together 10 years ago or so. Here's the small bio on Martin. "....He suffered terribly with asthma, struggling to get his b
2 CONC reath and had to use an inhaler. He lived with Axel and Delia (his sister, my great-grandma) before he got married. Axel would dole out Martin's inheritance money a little at a time because Martin would drink too much and fritter 
2 CONC it away otherwise. He finally straightened himself out and bought a small acreage. He appreciated Axel's concern. He married Sina Okland on 8 Sep 1908. She died 4 Jan 1954....". This is what I have for him. I hope it gives you som
2 CONC e comfort that he perhaps "straightened out" later on - as I'm still trying to do the same! Just ask my wife!! :-). I guess we're all trying to get our lives in order in one aspect or another! If you have an interest, I can send y
2 CONC ou a link to the tree, and let you view your living relatives, as they are otherwise noted as "Private". FYI, Amos and I appear to be 1st cousins 2x removed. Thanks much, from your cousin Dave! (David Nichols)
