2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-OYYV6ASTDEZD5AA6N3RZ6MGGQ47JX4Y-2-55396/myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-bef4a7d44a347280de5844cdd80481cc&mrid=62ba8548caf69b4e056ff47830de119d MyHeritage 
2 CONC Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 6 2026, 20:03:41 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lanesboro Leader Oct 31 1935
2 CONT Funeral services will be held tomorrow afternoon for Lars Topness aged 78 years who died last Monday morning at his farm home south of Highland.  Services at the home will be at 1:30 and at the Elstad Lutheran church at 2:15, the 
2 CONC Rev. N. S. Magelssen officiating.  Burial will be in the church cemetery.
2 CONT Mr. Topness, one of Fillmore county's oldest farmers, spent his entire life here.  He was born near Highland on Jan. 10, 1857, the son of Mr. and Mrs. Sylvester Topness who had emigrated from Norway.  The home he was born in is ju
2 CONC st about a mile from the one in which he died.
2 CONT Survivors include his wife, one brother, two sisters, two sons, two daughters, twelve grandchildren and three great grandchildren.  His brother, Tollef, named after an older brother who had died in early childhood, and his two sis
2 CONC ters, Mrs. Chas. Lawston of Leeds, N. D. and Mrs. Betsy Kolstad of Highland survive him.  A third brother, Sevren and two sisters, Sophia and Annie preceded him in death.
2 CONT Of his six children, four survive him, Henry and Clara, having died in early childhood.  His first wife, Betsy Nepstad Topness, who died many years ago was the mother of two of the living children, Mrs. Alma Beck of Amherst and Lo
2 CONC uis Topness, of Baker N. D. The surviving wife, Mrs. Karen Dammen Topness, is the mother of the two children who died in early childhood and of Mrs. Adolph Peterson of Lanesboro and Selmer L. Topness of Highland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elstad Lutheran Church burial records, p. 239 #11, Lars Topness 78 aar died 28 Okt 1935 buried 1 Nov 1935 at Elstad born at Elstad Text: 3rd artikel Note: Kræft.
