1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lanesboro Leader May 10 1945
2 CONT Mrs. Betsy Kolstad, Highland resident of many years, died early Friday morning, May 4 at the Lutheran Hospital in La Crosse where she had been a patient the past month.
2 CONT She was 81 years old and was born on the old homestead a mile and a half south of Highland on October 10, 1863, the daughter of Sylvester and Bertha Topness.
2 CONT As a young girl she moved with an older sister to northern Minnesota.  In 1879 she married Michael Kolstad who died in 1906.  They lived in Polk county for several years and returned 54 years ago to Highland where they purchased a
2 CONC  home.  She had resided there since except for a few years in Lanesboro.
2 CONT Survivors are an adopted daughter, Mrs. Hans Paulson of Lanesboro with whom she had made her home the past winter.  A sister, Mrs. Chas. Lawston of Clermont, Iowa, a brother, Tollef Topness of Dallas, Wis., four grandchildren, Law
2 CONC rence Paulson with the Marines somewhere in the Pacific, Vernon Paulson of Austin, Mrs. Edw. Kozlowski, White Bear Lake and Mrs. Jerome Ostrem of Lanesboro, also six great grandchildren and several nieces and nephews.
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted Sunday at 2 p.m. at the Hans Paulson home and at 3 p.m. from the Elstad Lutheran church.  Her pastor, Rev. N. S. Magelssen officiating.  Rev. A. O. Nesset, Clermont, Iowa, spoke in behalf of the fam
2 CONC ily.
2 CONT Interment was in the Elstad cemetery and pallbearers, all former meighbors, were Olaf Rustad, Minor Johnson, Lewis Olson, Tom Torgerson, Francis Johnson and Nat Shattuck.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elstad Lutheran Church baptism records, p. 32 #397, Betzy Camilla born 10 Octbr 1863 baptized 24 Januar 1864 at Elstad Parents: Sølfest Tollefsen o H. Berte Larsdatter Sponsors: Bertel Toresen, Sofie Bertelsdtr., Hanna do, Berte L
2 CONC arsd., Helge Aslaksen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elstad Lutheran Church confirmation records, p. 313 #21, confirmed 02 Dec 1878 Betsy Camilla Sølfestsdatter born 10/10 1863 baptized 24/1 1864 at Elstad Sølfest Tollefsen, Berthe Larsdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT Elstad Lutheran Church burial records, p. 1 #4, Mrs. Betsy Kolstad died May 4 1945 buried May 6 1945 at Elstad born at Elstad congregation Oct 10 1863 Parents: Sylvester & Bertha Topness Spouse: Michael Kolstad 1879 Note: Died at 
2 CONC the Luth. Hosp. in La Crosse.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/85149783/betsy_camilla-kolstad Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 6 2026, 20:13:09 UTC''
