2 CONT Burial record and obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/77286338/johanna-tobia-halverson
2 CONT
2 CONT Born/Christened: Johanna Tobia Jonasdtr/Johnsdatter, she is "Belle" Johnson in America
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary for Belle Johnson Halverson (Marshalltown Times Republican July 31, 1946)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Halver Halverson Dies at Home in City
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Halver Halverson, 69, died at 2 a.m. Wednesday at her home, 801-1.2 South Center Street. She had been in failing health for several years and death was due to a complication of ailments.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Halverson was born Belle Johnson, June 2, 1877, in Stavanger, Norway the daughter of John and Thelma Johnson. In 1901 she came to the United States and settled near LeGrand. On July 22 of that year she was married to Halver H
2 CONC alverson and the couple established a home at LeGrand. They moved to a farm six miles south of Marshalltown in 1920 and after living there six years moved to the present home here.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Halverson was preceded in death by two brothers and one sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving, beside the widower, are the two brothers, Ole and Omar Johnson of Marshalltown; three sisters, Christina Halverson of this city, and two sisters in Norway; three sons, Henry of Dunbar, Jesse and Harry of this city; thre
2 CONC e daughters, Mrs. Alva Kelsey of this city, Mrs. Harold Beisnecker, State Center, and Mrs. Wilbur Marshall of Waterloo; 25 grandchildren and 5 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. Friday at the Estel funeral home. Burial will be in Pleasant Hill Cemetery.
