2 CONT Occupation: farmer
2 CONT Comment: inducted at Fessenden on Sept. 18, 1917; sent to Camp Dodge, Iowa; served in Battery C, 338th Field Artillery, to Nov. 30, 1917; Battery F, 335th Field Artillery, to June 11, 1918; June Automatic Replacement Draft, Camp M
2 CONC erritt, N. J., to July 13, 1918; Battery F, 18th Field Artillery, to discharge; overseas from June 20, 1918, to April 28, 1919. Engagements: Offensives: Aisne-Marne; St. Mihiel; Meuse-Argonne. Defensive: Champagne-Marne. Defensive
2 CONC  Sectors: Vesle and Chateau-Thierry (Champagne). Discharged at Camp Dodge, Iowa, on June 10, 1919, as a Private.
