2 CONT
2 CONT Clarence Benjamin Nystuen, 90, died Saturday, January 28, 2006 in Payson, Arizona. Clarence was born November 13, 1915 in Northfield, Minnesota to Eliam and Emma Nystuen. The family attended Bethel Lutheran Church, founded by his 
2 CONC Grandfather, John T. Nystuen. He attended a neighborhood one-room schoolhouse through 8th grade and then attended Northfield High School, graduating in 1935. While still in High School, he and his older brother, Maurice, took over
2 CONC  the family farm. Clarence was an innovative farmer, always ready to try the newest equipment and methods.  Clarence married Betty Batson of Castle Rock, Minnesota on March 20, 1947. They had 3 daughters while in Minnesota. Claren
2 CONC ce was involved in the Northfield Saddle Club, serving as President for several years. In 1959, Clarence and Betty sold the family farm, moving to Montana briefly, where their 4th daughter was born. They then settled in Casa Grand
2 CONC e, Arizona where Clarence sold farm machinery for Bingham Equipment for the next 25 years. After retiring in 1985, Clarence and Betty moved to Payson, Arizona where Clarence spent his time collecting antiques, shopping at yard sal
2 CONC es and visiting with friends, neighbors and out-of-town guests. He was a life-long Republican. Clarence is survived by Betty, his wife of almost 59 years; three daughters: Becky Alvizo, Carol Nystuen and Linda Nystuen; six grandch
2 CONC ildren: Elizabeth Alvizo and Joanna Duncan, Steve Wilson, Sonja Wilson, Bethany and Jennifer Benedict; one great-grandson, Jerris Duncan. He was preceded in death by his parents; daughter Pamela Betty Nystuen; two brothers: Elmer 
2 CONC and Maurice Nystuen; two sisters: Mabel Arneson and Helen Miller.  A memorial service was held at Payson United Methodist Church, Payson, AZ. A memorial service was also held in Northfield, MN.  Source: Published in The Arizona Re
2 CONC public on Feb. 2, 2006.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.legacy.com/obituaries/azcentral/obituary.aspx?n=clarence-benjamin-nystuen&pid=16570904
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarence Benjamin Nystuen, 90, died Saturday, January 28, 2006 in Payson, Arizona. Clarence was born November 13, 1915 in Northfield, Minnesota to Eliam and Emma Nystuen. The family attended Bethel Lutheran Church, founded by his 
2 CONC Grandfather, John T. Nystuen. He attended a neighborhood one-room schoolhouse through 8th grade and then attended Northfield High School, graduating in 1935. While still in High School, he and his older brother, Maurice, took over
2 CONC  the family farm. Clarence was an innovative farmer, always ready to try the newest equipment and methods. Clarence married Betty Batson of Castle Rock, Minnesota on March 20, 1947. They had 3 daughters while in Minnesota. Clarenc
2 CONC e was involved in the Northfield Saddle Club, serving as President for several years. In 1959, Clarence and Betty sold the family farm, moving to Montana briefly, where their 4th daughter was born. They then settled in Casa Grande
2 CONC , Arizona where Clarence sold farm machinery for Bingham Equipment for the next 25 years. After retiring in 1985, Clarence and Betty moved to Payson, Arizona where Clarence spent his time collecting antiques, shopping at yard sale
2 CONC s and visiting with friends, neighbors and out-of-town guests. He was a life-long Republican. Clarence is survived by Betty, his wife of almost 59 years; three daughters: Becky Alvizo of Casa Grande, Carol Nystuen of Tempe, and Li
2 CONC nda Nystuen of Casa Grande; six grandchildren: Elizabeth Alvizo and Joanna Duncan of Tucson, Steve Wilson of Tempe, Sonja Wilson of Flagstaff, Bethany and Jennifer Benedict of Casa Grande; one great-grandson, Jerris Duncan of Tucs
2 CONC on; and many favorite nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his parents; daughter Pamela Betty Nystuen; two brothers: Elmer and Maurice Nystuen; two sisters: Mabel Arneson and Helen Miller, all of Minnesota. A memorial s
2 CONC ervice is scheduled for High Noon on Saturday, February 4 at Payson United Methodist Church, 414 N Easy Street, Payson, AZ 85541. A memorial service will also be held in Northfield, Minnesota at a later date. In lieu of flowers, p
2 CONC lease send donations to: Payson Kids, 300 W Wade Lane, Payson, AZ 85541, or your favorite charity. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Arizona Republic on Feb. 2, 2006
