1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/84849337/irving-guy-gaard
2 CONT
2 CONT Irving Guy Gaard, 91, was born on Oct. 8, 1906 to Amelia Urness and Alfred Gaard in Blue Earth, MN. He died on Sept 13, 1998 in North Branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Irving's first wife, Leona Olson, preceded him in death on Oct. 27, 1935. He married Nina Hendrickson on Dec. 17, 1940. He served in the Pacific Theatre in WW11. He was a farmer and carpenter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Irving is survived by his wife, Nina; and by sons: Irving (Arabelle) Jorgenson of Mesa, AZ and Richard (Marlene) Burtness of Caledonia; daughter, Ardys Kathy Kelly of Downy, CA; six grandchildren; 15 great-grandchildren; 12 great-
2 CONC great grandchildren; two sisters: Stella Girard and Fern Potter, both of Chino, CA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were on Sept. 15 at Spring Lake Lutheran church in North Branch, with the Rev. Robert Grendahl officiating. Crystal Peterson played the organ; Jon Ekstrom sang. Honorary casketbearers were: Raymond Medin and Stanl
2 CONC ey Sybrandt. Interment was in the Church cemetery.
