1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LANESBORO -- The funeral for Sidney M. Topness, 92, will be at 1 p.m. Wednesday at Elstad Lutheran Church in rural Lanesboro, with the Rev. Wade E. Davick officiating. Burial will be in Elstad Lutheran Church Cemet
2 CONC ery. 
2 CONT Mr. Topness, a longtime resident of the Lanesboro area, died Sunday (Sept. 30, 2007) at Harmony Healthcare. 
2 CONT Sidney Milford Topness was born May 18, 1915, in rural Whalan, Amherst Township, Fillmore County. He married Borghild Topness on Dec. 23, 1938, at the church parsonage. Mr. Topness farmed in Amherst Township until moving to Lanesb
2 CONC oro in 1979. He worked for the Lanesboro Public Utilities Light Plant, was a janitor at Elstad Lutheran Church, and opened graves in the Elstad Church cemetery for nine years. A lifelong member of Elstad Lutheran Church, he helped
2 CONC  carry on the church's mission. 
2 CONT Survivors include his wife; two sisters, Minerva (Arnold) Thompson of La Crescent and Isabel Johnson of Rushford. He was preceded in death by two brothers. 
2 CONT Visitation will be from 5 p.m. to 7 p.m. Tuesday at Johnson-Riley Funeral Home in Lanesboro, and an hour before the service Wednesday at the church.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21862743/sidney_milford-topness 
2 CONC Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 6 2026, 20:15:02 UTC''
