1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ione Roselyn Lightly, 97, formerly of Austin, passed away Tuesday, Jan. 28, 2014, in Peoria, Ill.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ione was born June 21, 1916, in rural Fillmore County, to Lars and Petra (Larson) Osland. Ione married Arnold Lightly on Oct 9, 1941. They had two children, Dorothy and Douglas. After graduating from Leroy High School in 1932, Io
2 CONC ne went to nurses' training at Swedish Hospital in Minneapolis, graduating in 1938. She worked at St. Olaf Hospital in Austin from 1938-1941. Ione and Arnold farmed in Oakland Township in Freeborn County.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She taught preschool Sunday school at First Baptist and Grace Baptist Churches in Austin.
2 CONT
2 CONT  After living on the family farm until 1985, Ione lived at St. Mark's Apartments in Austin for 27 years. She lived in Peoria, Ill., with Doug and Jane since 2012.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She was preceded in death by her husband in 1990, her daughter, Dorothy Davidson in 2011, her parents, two sisters, "Little Anna" and Anna Fairchild and three brothers, Orvin, Linsworth and Harold Osland.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ione is survived by her son, Douglas (Jane) Lightly of Peoria, Ill.; son-in-law, Don (Kathy) Davidson of Austin; five grandchildren, Dennis (Gwen) Davidson, Debbie (Cecil) Berlie, Lisa (Shaun) Carter, John (Ami) Lightly and David
2 CONC  (Rebekah) Lightly. She is also survived by eight great-grandchildren; one brother, Edward (Ramona) Osland of Waterloo, Iowa; sister-in-law, Evelyn Osland of Leroy; and nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. Saturday, Feb. 1, at the Clasen-Jordan Mortuary Chapel in Austin, with Pastor Gene Murrell officiating. Interment will be at Oakwood Cemetery. Visitation will be at the mortuary on Saturda
2 CONC y from 9:30 a.m. until the time of the service.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Memorials may be made to Moody Radio Ministry, or Shepherds Ministries in Union Grove, Wis.
2 CONT
2 CONT  - See more at: http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/postbulletin/obituary.aspx?pid=169426437#sthash.QdOI1bwz.dpuf
