2 PLAC Haven Home 
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wahoo
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Linsworth A. Osland  
2 CONT
2 CONT       YUTAN - Linsworth Alwood Osland, 86, died Aug. 27 at the South Haven Home in Wahoo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Osland was born on Feb. 3, 1920 to Lars and Petra (Larson) Osland near Chester, Iowa. He attended District 106 through the eighth grade and graduated from Chester High School in 1938. He was inducted into the United States Army Ai
2 CONC r Corp on Oct. 6, 1941 and served as a Quartermaster until Sept. 17, 1945. During his service he spent time as the assistant manager for the Military Gas Station at Laredo Army Air Base in Laredo, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He married Hazel Jacobson on Nov. 4, 1950 at the Salem Lutheran Church in Minneapolis, Minn. The couple lived in Minnesota before moving to Nebraska, first Omaha then Yutan. He was an electrician and a custom farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT       He served on councils at both Bethlehem Lutheran Church in Chester, Iowa and LeRoy Lutheran Church in Minnesota and was a member of the Yutan American Legion Post 262.
2 CONT
2 CONT       He was preceded in death by his parents, his wife, brothers, Orvin and Harold Osland and sisters, Anna Marge and Anna Marie.
2 CONT
2 CONT       He is survived by daughters and sons-in-law, Dixie and Randy Trost of Yutan and Cindy Osland and Mark Halvorson of Sidney, Mont.; son and daughter-in-law, Terry and Kelly Osland of Rogers, Minn.; grandchildren, Bryan and Ama
2 CONC nda Trost, Daniel and Kristi Trost, Lisa Trost, Linsi Osland and Mitchell Osland; great-grandchildren, Logan, Caleb and Julia Trost; brother and sister-in-law, Edward and Ramona Osland of Waterloo, Iowa and sister, Ione Lightly of
2 CONC  Austin, Minn.; sisters-in-law Ruth Osland of Adams, Minn., Evelyn Osland of LeRoy, Minn. and ViLee Jacobson of Ostrander, Minn.; and many nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Visitation will be held from 6 to 8 p.m. on Tuesday, Aug. 29 at St. John's Lutheran Church in Yutan. Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m., Thursday, Aug. 31 at LeRoy Lutheran Church in LeRoy, Minn. Interment will be at Ft
2 CONC . Snelling National Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Memorials may be made to either church.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Reichmuth Funeral Home of Yutan is in charge of the arrangements.
