1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=28117963
2 CONT
2 CONT                                                                            Nina VanDeWeerd 
2 CONT
2 CONT July 02, 2008 12:00 am
2 CONT
2 CONT (0) Signatures
2 CONT
2 CONT CRESCO - Nina VanDeWeerd, 89, of Cresco, died Monday, June 30, at Regional Health Services of Howard County.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born Jan. 19, 1919, on a homestead in Marshall County, Minn., daughter of Erwin and Anna Osland Hungerford. She married Marion J. VanDeWeerd on Jan. 9, 1946. He preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. VanDeWeerd taught in country schools for seven years before her marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by: three daughters, Carol (Paul) of Iowa City and Linda (Cyril) and Ruth, both of Davenport; two sons, Gary (Jen) and Robert (Sue), both of Cresco; five grandchildren; two great-grandsons; a brother, Louis (Mary Lou) Hun
2 CONC gerford of LeRoy, Minn.; two sisters-in-law, Wilma Hungerford of Galesburg, Ill., and Helen Hansen of Greeley, Colo.; and a brother-in-law, Bert VanDeWeerd of Cleveland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded in death by: two brothers, Elmer and Albert Hungerford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services: 11 a.m. Thursday at First Lutheran Church, with burial in Oak Lawn Cemetery, both in Cresco. Public visitation from 4 to 7 p.m. today at Lindstrom Funeral Home, Cresco, with a 6 p.m. Veterans of Foreign Wars Auxiliary se
2 CONC rvice. Visitation also an hour before services Thursday at the church.
