1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Sikkink&GSbyrel=in&GSdyrel=in&GSob=n&GSsr=121&GRid=122068680&
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Sikkink, 88, of Zumbrota, formerly of Preston, died January 18, 2004 at Zumbrota Health Care Services. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Bjortomt was born July 29, 1915, in Beaver Township, Fillmore County to Martin and Alma (Osterhus) Bjortomt. On January 28, 1939, she married Arden Sikkink in Harmony. The couple made their home and farmed in the Greenleafton
2 CONC /Preston area until moving to Zumbrota in 1957. They owned and operated the Zumbrota Bakery until 1965. Mrs. Sikkink then was executive housekeeper at Madonna Towers in Rochester until her retirement in 1978. Following her retirem
2 CONC ent, she cleaned houses for people in the area. Mr. Sikkink died July 25, 1999. She was an active member of United Redeemer Lutheran Church in Zumbrota and also was a member of the Zumbrota Hospital and Home Auxiliary, Zumbrota Se
2 CONC nior Citizens and Senior Citizens County Board. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include two daughters, Sharon (Arnie) Groszbach and Karen (Francis) Pflibsen, both of Zumbrota; one son, Alan (Arlys) of Zumbrota; six grandchildren; three great-grandchildren; one brother, Norman Bjortomt of Preston; an
2 CONC d three sisters, Verna Hahn of Zumbrota, LaVonne (Stanley) Wold of Lake City and Betty (Donald) Riehl of Preston. One brother preceded her in death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The memorial service for Ruth Sikkink was January 22, 2004 at United Redeemer Lutheran Church in Zumbrota, with the Rev. Clark Carey officiating. Burial was in Crown Hill Cemetery in Preston. Her body was cremated. Thauwald Funera
2 CONC l Home in Preston is in charge of arrangements.
