1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=58883043
2 CONT
2 CONT Evelyn Eiffler, 85, of Lime Springs, IA, passed away on Friday, September 17, 2010 at the Riceville Family Care Center in Riceville, IA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Evelyn was born on January 20, 1925 in York Towhship, Fillmore County, MN, on a farm called "White City". She was the daughter of Ernest A. and Mabel (Osterhaus) Stockdale. She was baptized on July 19, 1925 in the Bethlehem Luther
2 CONC an Church. She attended county school in Beaver Township District 106. She worked for her room board at $2.00 a week and attended LeRoy High School, graduating in June 1943. She worked in Minneapolis as a waitress for 6 months, an
2 CONC d as a waitress in Austin until she got called to work at Hormel's Packing Plant. After working there for three months, she returned home to care for her mother, who had turned sick. She worked for other families doing housework a
2 CONC nd chores.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Clarence Eiffler on July 25, 1944 at St. Paul's Lutheran Church She was confirmed at St. Paul's Lutheran Church on July 1, 1945. To this union two children were born, Betty and Duane. They lived on a farm near Davis Co
2 CONC rner's until they bought a farm in Howard Center in Howard County, IA in 1947. Clarence passed away on December 3, 1981. She continued to farm with her son. She was active in A.L.C.A., where she held the offices of secretary and t
2 CONC reasurer for 2 terms, as well as other positions. She taught Sunday School and sang in the Choir. She was a member of St. Paul's Lutheran Church, and belonged to and held offices in the Martha Circle, including President. Evelyn w
2 CONC as also a long time member of the American Legion Aux.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following Clarence's illness she became overwhelmed caring for both her husband and her mother who passed away on October 11, 1982.
2 CONT
2 CONT Evelyn is survived by her son, Duane (Irene) Eiffler of Lime Springs, IA, a daughter Betty Jean (Roger) Buchholtz of Elkader, IA, six grandchildren, 6 great-grandchildren, two sisters, Margaret (Raymond) Anderson of Fredericksburg
2 CONC , IA, and Thelma (Don) Holmen of Dexter, MN, along with several nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents, her husband, and three brothers, Louis, Vernon, and Glenn Stockdale.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lindstrom Funeral Home
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Pleasant Hill Cemetery  Lime Springs Howard County Iowa, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Diane Zabel Record added: Sep 19, 2010  Find A Grave Memorial# 58883043 
